            <div xml:id="d657">

                <pb facs="0793" n="785" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg785"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.635 Neep/62: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-04-21T07:00:00-00:44">April 21, 1938—7
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. I have informed President Barclay orally of contents of first 3 paragraphs
                    your telegram No. 13, April 12, noon. He is considering <pb facs="0794" n="786"
                        xml:id="pg786"/> the suggestion in paragraph 2 and I am awaiting his
                    decision; he states that he much prefers line suggested in paragraph 3.</p>
                <p>I inquired about preliminary report referred to in paragraph 4 which I am now
                    informed is dated March 6, 1935, and signed by H. Terpstra and V. D. Hoff.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
